This licence covers af-product-management material adapted from
MIT-licensed upstream product discovery and market research skills:
the skills opportunity-solution-tree, interview-script,
identify-assumptions, prioritize-assumptions, design-experiments,
prioritize-features, customer-journey-map, market-sizing,
market-segments, user-segmentation and user-personas; the parts of
product-brainstorming (trio-ideation.md), synthesize-research
(interview-summary.md, feedback-at-scale.md), metrics-review
(dashboard-design.md and its good-metric criteria) and competitive-brief
merged from it; and the commands brainstorm (ideas and experiments
modes), discover, interview, setup-metrics, triage-requests,
analyze-feedback, competitive-analysis and research-users.

It also covers material adapted from the same upstream's product
strategy and execution skills: the skills ansoff-matrix,
pestle-analysis, porters-five-forces, swot-analysis, product-strategy,
product-vision, value-proposition, business-model (with its Lean Canvas
and Startup Canvas references), pricing-strategy (with its
monetization-models reference), team-okrs, user-stories, pre-mortem,
strategy-red-team, prioritization-frameworks, release-notes,
sprint-retro, stakeholder-map, summarize-meeting, test-scenarios and
dummy-dataset; the parts of write-spec (the lean eight-section PRD),
sprint-planning and roadmap-update (references/outcome-roadmap.md)
merged from it; and the commands market-scan, pricing, strategy,
generate-data, meeting-notes, plan-okrs, red-team-prd, sprint,
transform-roadmap, write-prd and write-stories.

